Anthropic raised at least $81.3 billion in its initial public offering Thursday, making it the biggest stock market debut of all time and reflecting the massive scale of the AI boom &#x2013;&#xA0;and earning at least one celebrity investor billions.

The company set its share price on Wednesday at $83 per share, well above the initial $70 and $78 per share initially expected, for 980 million shares. While its diluted $1.5 trillion valuation is lower than the loftier $2 trillion valuation estimate some analysts predicted over the summer, the IPO reflects strong investor demand in the company&#x2019;s legion of Claude products, including model variants for productivity tasks, business aides and coding. Elon Musk&#x2019;s SpaceX had the record for the largest IPO of all time at an initial $1.77 trillion valuation, though it raised less money, at $75 billion. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'The Odyssey' Oscar Blitz to Begin With Robert Downey Jr., Guillermo del Toro and Steven Spielberg as Moderators Matt Damon Reveals Wife Suffered a Brain Aneurysm and Had Surgery the 'Week Before the Oscars' Where 'Oppenheimer' Won Best Picture

Still, some analysts have expressed concerns shared by many in the public about AI's unwieldy nature, the cost of maintaining and growing models, and developers' potential inability to maintain control over their products.

&#x201C;Anthropic will need to sustain rapid growth while managing the enormous cost of developing and running its models, and there is still considerable uncertainty around how the competitive landscape and economics of generative AI will evolve,&#x201D;&#xA0;Morningstar senior equity analyst Malik Ahmed Khan said in a note Thursday, pricing the stock at $92 with a &#x201C;very high uncertainty&#x201D;&#xA0;rating. &#x201C;For investors considering the IPO, the key question is whether they are comfortable with that range of outcomes and have a sufficiently long-term horizon.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In its prospectus filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the company was clear that its work could risk human civilization as we know it. The stark declarations came as part of a 90-page risk report, one of the largest reports of such factors in recent memory. Snap&#x2019;s risk factors totaled roughly 30 pages, while

&#x201C;Concerns have been raised both within our organization and by other researchers, regulators, policymakers, and industry participants that sufficiently advanced AI systems could, if not developed, deployed, and operated with appropriate safeguards, oversight, and security measures, pose catastrophic or existential risks to humanity, particularly if such systems were misused, replicated, weaponized, or allowed to operate with a high degree of autonomy,&#x201D; the company wrote, following warnings from a group of current and former Anthropic researchers this summer that the technology posed such risks.

